BT
/F1 11 Tf
48 792 Td
15 TL
/F1 18 Tf
(IOS-XR Nettools MCP) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(User Guide for the authenticated, read-only network inspection service) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F1 13 Tf
(SERVICE OVERVIEW) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(The MCP service runs in a persistent Docker container on a4000 and exposes) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(native MCP streamable HTTP. It is loopback-bound by default and intended) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(to be reached through an encrypted SSH tunnel.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F1 13 Tf
(WHAT THE SERVICE DOES) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(- Exposes reviewed Cisco IOS-XR lab inspection tools through MCP.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(- Inspects inventory, interface and routing protocol state, deterministic) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(  device health, tickets, logs, metrics, and selected topology sources.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(- Reconstructs device commands from typed inputs and an allowlist.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(- Sanitizes raw device command text before MCP clients receive results.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(- Does not expose arbitrary commands, configuration mode, shell access,) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(  or network remediation capability.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(- Keeps active probes disabled by default.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F1 13 Tf
(CONNECT FROM A MAC) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(1. Create an encrypted tunnel and keep it running:) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   ssh -N -L 8000:127.0.0.1:8000 rami@a4000) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(2. Point an MCP streamable-HTTP client at:) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(3. Send this header with every MCP request:) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   Authorization: Bearer <token>) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Use the client's secret store or a local environment variable for the) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(token. Never commit, paste into a shared document, or embed it in source.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
