/F1 18 Tf
(OPERATIONAL NOTES) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(- Router access uses strict SSH host-key verification.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(- Tickets, evidence, admission state, and event state use a persistent) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(  Docker named volume and survive container restart.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(- Docker Compose restarts the service after host reboot.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(- NetBox and Neo4j use Docker service DNS when their backing services run.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(  A stopped backing service returns a structured MCP error.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(- External-source tools depend on their platform services being available.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F1 13 Tf
(SUPPORT CHECKLIST) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(1. Confirm the SSH tunnel is running.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(2. Confirm the MCP client is sending the bearer token.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(3. Call list_lab_devices before a device-specific tool.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(4. For an object refusal, refresh the relevant device check and verify) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   that the requested object exists in current evidence.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(5. For NetBox or graph errors, verify the corresponding backing service) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   before changing MCP configuration.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F1 13 Tf
(CURRENT SERVICE CHARACTERISTICS) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(- 37 MCP tools are exposed on the classic surface.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(- Device inspection tools are read-only and command allowlisted.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(- Raw command output is withheld or sanitized at the MCP boundary.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(- The service is reachable from a Mac through the SSH tunnel above.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(This guide intentionally omits bearer tokens, router credentials,) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(and internal secret values.) Tj
ET
endstream
